## SECTION 5 — AUDIENCE INTELLIGENCE

**Who they are:** Mostly mums searching on behalf of their 8-10 year old daughter, not the child herself. Secondary searcher: mums planning a birthday/sleepover nail party for a group of same-age girls.

**What they want:** A visual idea dump to show her daughter, plus quiet reassurance nothing chosen will damage tiny nails or look "too old."

**What frustrates them:** Design lists that skip the safety question entirely (forcing a second-tab search); outdated defaults (unicorn, mermaid) that miss what girls actually pin now (preppy, smiley, coquette).

**Top 5 pain points:**
1. Uncertainty over whether gel/acrylic/UV lamp is safe at this age (actively debated even among "experts")
2. Wanting the look to feel "grown up enough" for a 9-10 year old without tipping into inappropriate/too-mature territory
3. Needing something that survives active play — sport, school, swimming — not just looks pretty in a photo
4. Not knowing what's actually trending right now vs. dated kids'-nail clichés
5. Planning for a specific occasion (birthday, party, back-to-school) and wanting designs matched to that moment

**Exact user phrases (from real Pinterest/forum/Lemon8 language):**
